-- A member whose balance is below zero is delinquent, and gets a flag while delinquent. Rule
-- FlagMember fires in the commit of every Charge. `velle validate` passes, and prints three A5
-- advisories under "What the compiler advises". The first is:
--
--   - [A5] every commit touching Member joins a single queue. Reads Member.balance with no path back to any key (rule FlagMember), so any two such commits conflict. State the policy:
--     - correlate the read (relate Member to the shape that partitions it), or
--     - move the rule to a schedule (`on <Schedule>`) — the read then runs once per tick instead of inside every commit, or
--     - declare `tolerates contention` on the rule FlagMember (OQ40)
--
-- The other two, for Flag ("Consults OpenFlag through a path the derivation cannot key") and
-- Resolution ("Consults Resolution through a path the derivation cannot key"), end the same
-- way, "declare `tolerates contention` on the rule FlagMember (OQ40)". OQ40 is a settled
-- question in `working-docs/QUESTIONS.md` and means nothing to the author reading the advisory.
-- `compiler/CLAUDE.md` "Diagnostics" says a diagnostic is read by a Velle author and carries no
-- internal vocabulary; "the derivation cannot key" is internal vocabulary too. The parser does
-- the same in `43-tolerates-names-oq-tag-refused.velle`.
act Member {
    name: text
    balance: decimal
}

transient act Charge {
    member: one Member
    amount: decimal
}

rule ApplyCharge when Charge {
    member.balance = member.balance - amount
}

shape Delinquent = Member where balance < 0

shape Flag { member: one Member }

shape Resolution { flag: one Flag }

shape OpenFlag = Flag where not exists Resolution for this

rule FlagMember when (Delinquent where not exists OpenFlag for this) {
    Flag from { member: this }
}

rule ResolveFlag when leaving Delinquent {
    Resolution from { flag: (OpenFlag for this) }
}
